# Team Hub Project Rules

## Purpose
- Keep agent changes small, safe, and consistent with current architecture.

## Project context
- Runtime flow: `ui-web -> gw-nginx -> gw-api -> srv-auth|srv-organization|srv-notification` (auth also uses `db-postgres` + `cache-redis`; org→notification via Kafka `msg-kafka`).
- Compose/Aspire service names follow `[type]-[module]` (`srv-*`, `gw-*`, `ui-*`, `db-*`, `cache-*`, `msg-*`, `mon-*`, `blob-storage`).
- Code folders stay as `services/team-hub-*` / `frontend/team-hub-web`; runtime DNS names use the convention above.

## Source of truth
- `docker-compose.yml`
- `docker-compose.dev.yml`
- `infrastructure/nginx/nginx.conf`
- `infrastructure/redis/docker-compose.redis.yml`
- `infrastructure/kafka/docker-compose.kafka.yml`
- `building-blocks/TeamHub.Redis/*`
- `building-blocks/TeamHub.Kafka/*`
- `services/team-hub-gateway/team-hub-gateway/reverseproxy.json`
- `services/team-hub-gateway/team-hub-gateway/appsettings.*.json`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Controllers/AuthController*.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/.env.example` (local dev + docker compose)
- `services/team-hub-gateway/team-hub-gateway/.env.example` (docker compose; JWT when AuthValidation enabled)
- `services/team-hub-organization/team-hub-organization/Program.cs`
- `docs/README.mb` and related `docs/*.mb`
- Component `AGENT.md` files in each service and frontend

## Do
- Route auth API through gateway path `/api/auth/{**catch-all}`.
- Route organization API through gateway path `/api/organizations/{**catch-all}`.
- Route notification API through gateway path `/api/notifications/{**catch-all}`.
- Keep auth endpoints aligned with controllers: `register`, `login`, `refresh`, `logout`.
- Docker compose is for Production-like pre-deployment builds (`ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production`, per-service `.env` files).
- Local dev database: `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d` (`team-hub-dev`, service `db-postgres`, databases `auth_db` / `organization_db` / `notification_db`, volume `postgres_data_dev`).
- Use documented ports/env from config (`8080`, `5000`, `5001`, `5002`, `5004`, `4200`, `5433`) and verify before edits.
- Update docs in `docs/` and component `AGENT.md` when API contract, ports, or runtime flow changes.
- Prefer minimal diffs and preserve existing naming/style in touched files.

## Don't
- Do not bypass infrastructure nginx or gateway in frontend integration.
- Do not invent routes, env vars, or services not present in config/code.
- Do not run destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, forced history rewrites).
- Do not modify unrelated files outside the requested scope.

## Definition of done
- Change solves the requested task with smallest safe diff.
- Affected paths/config references are validated against source files.
- Relevant tests/checks are run when code behavior changes.
- Documentation is updated if behavior or contract changed.
